infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Heap profile: inuse_space vs alloc_space
  desc Two views of the same data — choosing wrong wastes an afternoon
  compares
    - label inuse_space — what is retained
      children
        - label Bytes currently live
          desc Attributed to the allocation site — answers "what is filling memory?"
        - label Leaks, caches, retention
          desc One giant retained slice dominates inuse while allocating little
        - label The leak metric: diff two snapshots
          desc pprof -base subtracts the stable heap and names the growing site
    - label alloc_space — what generates GC pressure
      children
        - label Cumulative bytes ever allocated
          desc Counts every byte since start — never decreases, says nothing about retention
        - label Churn, GC pressure
          desc The fmt boxing of earlier lessons: allocate-and-drop
        - label 4 TB cumulative, zero retained
          desc A 50 MB/s hot path reaches 4 TB in a day while holding nothing
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
